# Git Commit Messages

All commits must start with a [gitmoji](https://gitmoji.dev/) emoji followed by a short imperative description.

## Format

```
<emoji> <short description>

[optional body]
```

## Common Emojis

| Emoji | Code | Use for |
|---|---|---|
| ✨ | `:sparkles:` | New features |
| 🐛 | `:bug:` | Bug fixes |
| ♻️ | `:recycle:` | Refactoring |
| ⬆️ | `:arrow_up:` | Upgrade dependencies |
| 🎨 | `:art:` | Code structure / formatting |
| 📝 | `:memo:` | Documentation |
| 🔧 | `:wrench:` | Config files |
| 🏷️ | `:label:` | Types |
| 🧑‍💻 | `:technologist:` | Developer experience |
| 🩹 | `:adhesive_bandage:` | Simple non-critical fix |
| 🔥 | `:fire:` | Remove code or files |
| 💄 | `:lipstick:` | UI / styles |

## Examples

```bash
# ✅ Good
git commit -m "✨ add idle gold accumulation mechanic"
git commit -m "⬆️ bump Next.js to v15 and React to v18"
git commit -m "🐛 fix equipment slot overwriting on purchase"
git commit -m "♻️ extract monster hp logic into helper"

# ❌ Bad
git commit -m "fix stuff"
git commit -m "WIP"
git commit -m "updates"
```

Full emoji reference: https://gitmoji.dev/
